<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pescennius Niger</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 135–194</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century">2nd century</a> · Also known as Gaius Pescennius Niger</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pescennius <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> was governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> who was proclaimed emperor by his troops in 193 CE, in the civil war after the murder of Pertinax. Supported by the eastern provinces and by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>, he was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/septimius-severus">Septimius Severus</a> at Cyzicus, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a> and finally Issus in 194 and killed. Byzantium held out against Severus' siege until about 196.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pescennius-niger.jpg" alt="Pescennius Niger" width="320" height="331" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Numismatica Ars Classica NAC AG · CC BY-SA 3.0 ch · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aureus_Pescennius_Niger_(obverse).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
